{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>עד</b> — Until now he rebukes the judges, that they are elohim [i.e., divine beings], <b>until when will you judge injustice</b>, for the power of HaShem is in the angels through action." "<b>And you lift the faces of the wicked</b> — the opposite of: <b>your faces fell</b>; therefore after it: <b>surely if you do well, you lift</b>."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 82, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:47.767086512Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}